WEBVTT

00:46.212 --> 00:47.505
Can you stay over?

00:50.675 --> 00:54.179
This is why…
this is why we had to break up.

00:54.262 --> 00:55.889
NOVEMBER, 2008

00:56.973 --> 00:58.558
Yeon-su, let's grab a bite.

00:58.641 --> 01:01.311
Oh, sorry. I'm not too hungry right now.

01:01.394 --> 01:03.938
Oh, come on. I'll get you banana milk.
Come on.

01:04.022 --> 01:05.523
No, really, I'm fine. It's okay.

01:05.607 --> 01:07.317
- You can go ahead. It's cool.
- Okay.

01:07.400 --> 01:09.402
Yo, Ji-yeon, hurry up.
Let's get a move on.

01:10.487 --> 01:11.571
I'll see you.

01:11.654 --> 01:13.198
Come on, hurry up!

01:13.281 --> 01:15.742
Not like she'll ever come.
Why bother, right?

01:15.825 --> 01:17.452
Keep it down. She can hear you.

01:17.535 --> 01:18.703
Why do you care about her so much?

01:18.787 --> 01:20.914
That self-centered princess
doesn't like you.

01:20.997 --> 01:22.582
She doesn't even know you exist.

01:22.665 --> 01:23.958
She's right. Think about it.

01:24.042 --> 01:26.127
Yeon-su's never bothered
treating us or anything.

01:26.211 --> 01:27.462
We always bought her stuff.

01:27.545 --> 01:30.632
Still, it wasn't like she asked us
to buy her any of those things.

01:30.715 --> 01:32.092
It's called being shameless.

01:32.175 --> 01:35.095
She still accepted them
every single time without hesitation.

01:35.178 --> 01:38.056
Remember the last time?
You always gave her a birthday gift…

01:38.139 --> 01:40.100
I absolutely hate being poor.

01:40.683 --> 01:43.853
The worst part is,
I can't be generous or return favors.

01:46.648 --> 01:49.025
Our family's been poor
ever since I was born.

01:49.109 --> 01:50.193
I didn't do it.

01:50.276 --> 01:51.736
I didn't do it either.

01:51.820 --> 01:53.696
Whatever. It's cool.
Don't worry about it.

01:53.780 --> 01:56.449
It made making real friends
or hanging out with them 

01:56.533 --> 01:58.243
uncomfortably difficult.

02:01.746 --> 02:05.291
As a young girl, it was painful.
I'd always be hurting inside.

02:06.876 --> 02:08.378
But I guess it was okay.

02:10.046 --> 02:11.172
Grandma.

02:13.466 --> 02:17.137
You're here again. I told you not to come.
Just go straight home and wait for me.

02:17.220 --> 02:19.639
Are you kidding me?
You want me home alone, all bored?

02:19.722 --> 02:20.765
Good grief.

02:20.849 --> 02:24.227
It was okay, I had something
precious that I wanted to protect.

02:24.310 --> 02:26.896
You hands are freezing.
Have you eaten?

02:26.980 --> 02:28.439
Were you extra busy today?

02:28.523 --> 02:29.858
No, not at all.

02:30.859 --> 02:33.486
- Look at her skirt.
- She's obviously a teacher's pet.

02:33.570 --> 02:35.446
Hey, look at her shoes.
Even my mom wouldn't…

02:35.530 --> 02:37.740
That's why I decided
to completely ignore everyone.

02:37.824 --> 02:39.868
Call it being self-centered or whatever.

02:41.077 --> 02:43.121
Simply put, it was more convenient.

02:43.204 --> 02:45.623
I know a lot of you
are excited for spring.

02:46.207 --> 02:48.459
Despite the weather becoming much cooler,

02:48.543 --> 02:52.172
I would like to thank you all
for being here on this very special day.

02:52.255 --> 02:54.048
Hey. Turn around.

02:54.632 --> 02:56.009
Seeing all of you here,

02:56.092 --> 02:58.595
I remember standing
in the school field 34 years ago.

02:58.678 --> 03:01.306
I was like that all the way,
until I met Choi Ung.

03:02.724 --> 03:03.725
I'll kill you…

03:05.602 --> 03:08.646
If you tell anyone
that we're dating, I'll kill you.

03:10.356 --> 03:11.941
And I don't want you bothering me either.

03:12.025 --> 03:14.152
My studies and
getting into university come first.

03:14.986 --> 03:17.614
Likewise, same thing goes for you.
You got that?

03:18.615 --> 03:19.657
Okay.

03:24.621 --> 03:26.289
Is there anything you wanna say to me?

03:32.462 --> 03:33.546
Got plans tomorrow?

03:42.096 --> 03:44.599
The sole person
who helped me close my eyes

03:44.682 --> 03:46.267
and escape from reality,

03:47.352 --> 03:48.269
Choi Ung.

03:52.982 --> 03:54.692
- Did you sleep well?
- Mm-hmm.

03:55.401 --> 03:58.238
- How long did you wait?
- I didn't. I just got here.

04:00.990 --> 04:03.868
So they're both symbolic
and represent specific things.

04:04.661 --> 04:06.496
The difference between those two…

04:06.579 --> 04:09.207
"According to this,
the population of the village…"

04:11.292 --> 04:13.795
Why am I dozing off?

04:16.839 --> 04:19.133
- "Ever since the 1960s…"
- Mm-hmm.

04:19.968 --> 04:22.720
- "The rapid industrialization of…"
- Uh-huh.

04:23.972 --> 04:25.640
SEO-YEON UNIVERSITY
2012 ADMISSION RESULT

04:34.983 --> 04:37.026
CONGRATULATIONS

04:37.110 --> 04:38.861
NAME: CHOI UNG
MAJOR: ART AND DESIGN

04:50.915 --> 04:51.791
LET'S GO OUTSIDE

05:13.021 --> 05:14.689
LET'S GO OUTSIDE

05:26.200 --> 05:27.577
Yeon-su.

05:28.745 --> 05:29.787
What?

05:29.871 --> 05:32.040
- Man, what are you eating?
- Gimbap.

05:32.123 --> 05:34.542
Oh, well. So much for this then.

05:36.878 --> 05:39.422
Kimchi fried rice, cherry tomatoes.

05:39.505 --> 05:40.673
Did you really make this?

05:40.757 --> 05:43.217
Yeah, of course. Wasn't really that hard.

05:50.058 --> 05:52.602
- Not so great?
- No, it is.

05:53.936 --> 05:55.021
Exactly.

05:59.317 --> 06:02.028
No, I didn't. What are you talking about?

06:04.447 --> 06:05.740
When did I let my guard down?

06:05.823 --> 06:07.533
You were looking all excited
when those girls

06:07.617 --> 06:09.118
were acting really friendly around you.

06:09.202 --> 06:11.287
Tell them to show a little bit of respect.

06:12.372 --> 06:13.873
Yeah, yeah, I know.

06:13.956 --> 06:16.667
I'm just upset because you were
wasting your time with those kids.

06:16.751 --> 06:17.877
I'm sorry.

06:17.960 --> 06:19.212
Oftentimes,

06:20.171 --> 06:22.715
I was yearning for a relief
from the practicality of it all.

06:23.216 --> 06:24.300
COVER LETTER

06:24.384 --> 06:27.095
It gave me
that comforting escape from reality.

06:29.680 --> 06:30.556
Are you done?

06:31.182 --> 06:33.851
Not yet.
I still have a few left to send out.

06:33.935 --> 06:35.269
Do you need it right away?

06:36.187 --> 06:37.438
What do you mean?

06:37.522 --> 06:40.108
I mean, instead of getting a 9-to-5 job,

06:40.191 --> 06:42.610
you can continue to study more
and land a better job in the future.

06:42.693 --> 06:44.821
Except I don't have any time for that.

06:44.904 --> 06:47.824
I need to get a job right now,
gotta become a full-time employee.

06:49.075 --> 06:50.034
You get a job. Then what?

06:53.287 --> 06:56.374
Well, I'm going to save up money so

06:56.916 --> 06:58.668
my grandma won't have to work anymore.

06:59.168 --> 07:00.628
- Is that it?
- What?

07:01.963 --> 07:05.925
I mean, you managed to get scholarships,
while working part-time,

07:06.008 --> 07:08.553
you've been breaking your back
juggling studies and work.

07:08.636 --> 07:11.305
I just thought you'd be aiming
for something a little bigger than that.

07:18.646 --> 07:21.482
I wanna live
as well as the average person.

07:21.566 --> 07:23.943
That was my dream for the longest time.

07:26.779 --> 07:28.614
I consider that a success.

07:28.698 --> 07:32.535
Could it be
that maybe this isn't the dream I want?

07:32.618 --> 07:34.662
And you?
What do you plan to do afterwards?

07:35.997 --> 07:37.957
Me? Uhm…

07:38.040 --> 07:40.585
I don't really have a plan.

07:40.668 --> 07:42.795
You're good at drawing
and you enjoy doing it.

07:42.879 --> 07:44.130
You could do that for a living.

07:44.213 --> 07:47.216
I'm going to keep that as a hobby.

07:47.300 --> 07:48.176
What I want

07:48.259 --> 07:50.178
is to bask in the sun during the day

07:50.261 --> 07:52.513
and lay underneath a lamp
at night time. That's it.

07:52.597 --> 07:54.348
A stressful life just isn't for me.

07:56.058 --> 07:57.768
Perhaps it's destiny.

07:57.852 --> 08:00.229
I was never given a choice to begin with.

08:00.313 --> 08:02.440
To be honest,
I'm content with my life.

08:02.523 --> 08:03.816
I got my family and you.

08:10.448 --> 08:13.951
But life often slaps you awake
when you open your eyes.

08:19.540 --> 08:24.045
It's even more cruel,
that ruthless monster called reality.

08:24.128 --> 08:25.171
Why us?

08:26.631 --> 08:29.091
Why do we need to pay the debt instead?

08:30.384 --> 08:32.887
I've never even met…

08:32.970 --> 08:36.557
…this man who's…
who's supposedly my uncle.

08:37.350 --> 08:38.935
Yeon-su…

08:40.895 --> 08:41.938
Oh, my child.

08:43.814 --> 08:45.274
I really wish that…

08:48.945 --> 08:51.697
I was only poor enough
to the point that I…

08:52.532 --> 08:54.075
could at least handle it.

09:10.591 --> 09:11.634
We're going now.

09:17.557 --> 09:20.268
Reality sneered
at my false dreams.

09:22.478 --> 09:23.688
Hello, what is it?

09:28.442 --> 09:29.360
Yeon-su, wait!

09:29.902 --> 09:31.279
And before I knew it…

09:39.662 --> 09:43.082
…just like that,
it was suffocating the life out of me.

09:49.380 --> 09:50.464
I'm not gonna go.

09:52.842 --> 09:56.053
You do realize
this is every student's dream, right?

09:56.137 --> 09:58.639
Do you have any idea
how much talent you have?

09:58.723 --> 10:00.308
I'm sure you've noticed
that you've improved.

10:00.391 --> 10:02.852
And that's only
after being there for six months.

10:02.935 --> 10:05.104
Exactly, that was only six months.

10:05.187 --> 10:07.773
Living there for a few years,
that's a different story.

10:07.857 --> 10:10.443
Being there all by myself
isn't what I want.

10:10.526 --> 10:12.403
Seriously? Is that your reason, huh?

10:12.987 --> 10:15.364
Just think about it,
you can draw all the buildings you love,

10:15.448 --> 10:17.366
and you can push yourself even further.

10:19.201 --> 10:22.079
What's the matter?
Don't you have any ambition?

10:22.163 --> 10:24.040
No. I don't.

10:24.123 --> 10:27.126
I'm not interested in striving
for success or any of that crap.

10:28.127 --> 10:30.588
Someone more desperate
deserves that opportunity.

10:30.671 --> 10:33.007
Unbelievable.

10:41.265 --> 10:43.601
SEO-YEON UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
INPATIENT BILL

10:58.741 --> 11:01.577
Oh, wow. When did you get here?

11:02.119 --> 11:04.914
Something's different.
You don't normally wait for me at all.

11:06.082 --> 11:08.084
Are we gonna get lunch? What do you want?

11:08.918 --> 11:10.086
Wanna head out now?

11:19.845 --> 11:21.013
That's why…

11:22.098 --> 11:24.600
that's the reason
why we couldn't be together…

11:24.684 --> 11:27.019
Why do we have to break up?

11:30.564 --> 11:33.484
Because our realities
were just way too different.

11:33.567 --> 11:35.486
You always break up with me first.

11:37.029 --> 11:40.866
Rather, it was 'cause
my reality was pathetic.

11:40.950 --> 11:43.494
Am I the easiest thing to throw away

11:43.577 --> 11:45.204
among the things you have?

11:48.749 --> 11:49.875
No.

11:52.670 --> 11:54.130
But you're the only one…

11:55.005 --> 11:56.549
that I can get rid of.

12:02.096 --> 12:03.472
Why are you doing this?

12:04.265 --> 12:05.766
Come to think of it…

12:07.059 --> 12:11.731
maybe it was because
I couldn't even handle my own reality.

12:11.814 --> 12:13.149
Give me reason.

12:14.066 --> 12:15.359
To be honest…

12:16.610 --> 12:19.238
Give me just one reason
why we can't be together.

12:20.656 --> 12:24.160
To be completely honest, I was afraid

12:24.869 --> 12:29.373
someday you'd eventually notice
this inferiority complex of mine.

12:30.207 --> 12:37.047
EPISODE 6
PRIDE AND PREJUDICE

12:52.772 --> 12:55.608
I could have sworn
I was working in my studio.

13:32.436 --> 13:34.772
Jeez, you scared me to death!
What the hell!

13:34.855 --> 13:36.565
Don't sneak up on me like that.

13:36.649 --> 13:38.692
- When did you get here?
- Just a while ago.

13:38.776 --> 13:40.945
I thought you'd have trouble
sleeping again. I was worried.

13:42.238 --> 13:44.532
Sleep some more. You didn't get enough.

13:44.615 --> 13:46.450
Hey, what time did I go to bed?

13:46.534 --> 13:48.160
How the hell would I know that?

13:51.539 --> 13:53.332
How'd I doze off like that?

13:53.415 --> 13:55.626
- I can't believe I slept so well.
- Well, that's good to hear.

13:55.709 --> 13:58.420
Your stopwatch stopped
a bit over 10 p.m. last night.

13:58.504 --> 14:00.631
- Probably around then.
- Maybe.

14:00.714 --> 14:02.967
- Did you take sleeping pills?
- Hmm.

14:04.218 --> 14:06.679
I wondered why you slept
on the sofa instead of your bed.

14:10.015 --> 14:11.433
What is that thing?

14:20.150 --> 14:23.404
Bro, you completed 95 hours.

14:23.487 --> 14:25.322
Guess you must be
in your element.

14:25.406 --> 14:26.574
You look amazing today.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.868
Hey. What time did you get here again?

14:29.451 --> 14:30.911
Me? Around 7:30 a.m.

14:30.995 --> 14:32.204
Was I alone just then?

14:32.288 --> 14:33.497
- Wrong, bro.
- You mean…

14:33.581 --> 14:35.541
I meant not just then.
You've always been alone.

14:35.624 --> 14:36.917
- Oh, screw you.
- Oh, that's right.

14:37.001 --> 14:38.752
Ji-ung's gonna be dropping by
some time today,

14:38.836 --> 14:41.171
to edit the footage of you working.
Also, he's gonna be doing

14:41.255 --> 14:43.799
some filming here and there,
specifically the live drawing show.

14:43.883 --> 14:45.551
Let's show him
just how charming you can be.

14:45.634 --> 14:47.386
How awesome you look when you're drawing.

14:47.469 --> 14:49.388
You're no longer the pitiful boy, right?

14:50.306 --> 14:52.266
Are you listening?

14:53.225 --> 14:55.895
God, how long has it been
since I slept this well?

14:55.978 --> 14:58.188
That good, huh? Didn't wake up at all?

14:58.272 --> 15:00.316
- Mm-hmm.
- Good. That's great.

15:00.399 --> 15:02.651
That's really good.
Means you'll be in great condition.

15:05.487 --> 15:09.074
If that's true,
what's this unsettling feeling I have?

15:12.369 --> 15:14.955
Honey, it's the weekend,
what are you doing up so early?

15:15.039 --> 15:17.249
That opening ceremony
I've been working so hard on

15:17.333 --> 15:20.961
- these past few weeks is today.
- Oh, really? That's today?

15:21.045 --> 15:23.380
- Sit down, grandma.
- Oh, gosh.

15:23.464 --> 15:25.299
Time sure does fly fast.

15:25.382 --> 15:27.676
If you have some time later,
come and visit with grandma Ji-na.

15:27.760 --> 15:30.512
That's okay. I don't want to distract you.

15:30.596 --> 15:33.098
You've worked so hard on that project.

15:33.182 --> 15:35.184
I'm sure you did a fantastic job.

15:35.267 --> 15:37.269
You're the only person in the world
who appreciates me.

15:39.813 --> 15:42.900
Oh, this girl. You know what I heard?

15:43.692 --> 15:46.904
I heard somewhere that the welfare center,

15:46.987 --> 15:49.823
they're actually accepting
job application forms.

15:49.907 --> 15:51.575
I think I should give it a go.

15:51.659 --> 15:53.494
What? You're kidding me, right?

15:53.577 --> 15:55.579
You must be out of your mind. No way!

15:55.663 --> 15:58.499
Forget it. You're no spring chicken,
I'll tell you that.

15:58.582 --> 16:01.251
I'm bored. That's all.
It's driving me nuts.

16:01.335 --> 16:04.046
I'm stuck in the house all day,
it's sucking the life out of me.

16:04.129 --> 16:05.089
I'm gonna die of suffocation.

16:05.172 --> 16:08.384
There's plenty of stuff for you to do.
Hang out at the senior citizen center--

16:08.467 --> 16:10.719
No, thank you.
There's nothing for me there.

16:10.803 --> 16:12.054
Unless you want me to die of boredom.

16:12.137 --> 16:14.723
Just a bunch of sick, old people
waiting for death.

16:14.807 --> 16:16.600
That's the thing,
you should work on your temper.

16:16.684 --> 16:18.102
That's why you have no friends.

16:18.185 --> 16:20.729
What was that? You think
I'm some kind of rabid pit bull?

16:20.813 --> 16:23.148
Anyway, it doesn't matter.
Just thought I'd let you know.

16:23.232 --> 16:26.735
Come on. What if you collapse
in the middle of work?

16:26.819 --> 16:27.695
I can't…

16:29.154 --> 16:33.158
I'm afraid of staying home.
That's what'll ruin me mentally.

16:33.826 --> 16:36.620
What's the disease old people get, huh?

16:36.704 --> 16:37.746
Dementia, that one.

16:39.957 --> 16:42.835
Hey, I'm just being cautious.
I'm not demented yet.

16:42.918 --> 16:45.838
I'm clearheaded
compared to other people my age.

16:45.921 --> 16:49.508
Yeah, no one, I mean no one
can hold a candle to your grandma.

16:50.426 --> 16:52.136
So don't worry about a thing.

16:52.761 --> 16:54.138
Go and eat up.

16:56.056 --> 16:57.850
Not really worried or anything.

16:58.475 --> 17:01.020
Then why are you staring at me
like I'm about to croak?

17:01.103 --> 17:02.354
Not very comforting.

17:02.438 --> 17:05.399
I'm just upset
because it breaks my heart, you know.

17:05.482 --> 17:08.819
You've been working your entire life,
without so much as a vacation.

17:08.902 --> 17:10.487
Can't you just
take it easy once in a while?

17:10.571 --> 17:13.699
What are you talking about?
It doesn't get easier than this.

17:13.782 --> 17:16.618
You cook and prepare my meals
and everything else that I need.

17:16.702 --> 17:18.662
All I do is put my feet up.

17:18.746 --> 17:21.498
Oh, boy, it's so tough. Someone help me.

17:21.582 --> 17:23.125
I'm so exhausted.

17:23.208 --> 17:26.587
Now, go and eat up.
Enough with this nonsense.

17:28.630 --> 17:29.923
On one condition…

17:31.967 --> 17:33.594
don't do anything demanding.

17:34.720 --> 17:36.805
If you only have to work
for like a few hours a day,

17:36.889 --> 17:38.390
then fine, I'll think about it.

17:38.474 --> 17:41.143
You're acting ridiculous, hmm?

17:42.478 --> 17:46.648
Who do you think you are, young lady?
Do you want me to start calling you mom?

17:46.732 --> 17:49.860
Damn straight.
I'm pretty much your legal guardian.

17:50.527 --> 17:52.863
Better not cross me if you know
what's good for you, young lady.

17:55.282 --> 17:57.159
You should hear yourself.

17:57.242 --> 17:58.494
- Honey, wait.
- Huh?

17:58.577 --> 17:59.495
- Ho.
- Huh?

17:59.578 --> 18:01.955
- What in the world are you wearing?
- Chang-sik, look.

18:02.039 --> 18:03.665
- Not bad. What'd you think?
- This won't do.

18:03.749 --> 18:04.833
Go back and put the other necktie.

18:04.917 --> 18:06.794
The red one
will look better with this suit.

18:06.877 --> 18:08.670
Hi. Have you guys seen
the restaurant owners?

18:08.754 --> 18:10.214
They look like you,
but completely the opposite.

18:10.297 --> 18:12.341
I'm glad you're here. Look at us.

18:12.424 --> 18:14.426
Be honest. How do we look?
Tell us what you think.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.762
Overall, you look like
a couple of Hollywood producers

18:16.845 --> 18:18.806
who live in a wealthy neighborhood.

18:18.889 --> 18:21.475
I barely recognize you two.

18:21.558 --> 18:23.477
It's for a special occasion.

18:23.560 --> 18:25.604
Ung is going to be
putting on a performance.

18:25.687 --> 18:29.733
That boy's been constantly putting on
a performance 24-7 since he was a kid,

18:29.817 --> 18:31.568
don't know why
you have to get all dressed up for it.

18:31.652 --> 18:34.279
He's not gonna be putting on
some kind of an act, you jackass.

18:34.363 --> 18:36.156
Ung's gonna draw something special

18:36.240 --> 18:38.367
in front of a live audience
and there'll be a huge crowd.

18:38.450 --> 18:40.160
Eun-ho came by last time
and told us about it.

18:40.244 --> 18:41.620
He said we had to come.

18:41.703 --> 18:44.206
To think that our son
never even bothered inviting us.

18:44.289 --> 18:46.625
We still have a lot of time
before it starts, you know.

18:46.708 --> 18:49.044
We need to make sure
to sit at the front row.

18:49.128 --> 18:50.212
Oh, my goodness. Oh, my goodness.

18:50.295 --> 18:52.214
Wait. Honey, we need
to pick up the rice cakes!

18:52.297 --> 18:55.300
I almost forgot! We need to go so we can
pick up and give them the rice cakes.

18:55.384 --> 18:58.679
Wait. Trust me, you oughtta just
hand them out to your neighbors instead,

18:58.762 --> 19:00.097
unless you want him to faint out there.

19:00.180 --> 19:02.474
Still, we need to show
at least some sort of courtesy.

19:02.558 --> 19:04.268
They're going all the way over there

19:04.351 --> 19:05.561
- to watch him draw.
- That's right.

19:05.644 --> 19:08.313
Let me make this clear.
Those people need him more than you think.

19:08.397 --> 19:09.857
They practically begged him to draw.

19:09.940 --> 19:12.484
Everything's all set for him and
he'll pretty much be treated like a king.

19:12.568 --> 19:15.195
My goodness. Is that true?

19:16.071 --> 19:17.865
My gosh!

19:17.948 --> 19:19.366
Did you hear that, you fool, huh?

19:19.449 --> 19:22.411
They begged my son to draw for them.
He's important to all those people.

19:22.494 --> 19:24.413
Wait, that's why
he's drawing for them right?

19:24.496 --> 19:26.540
Yep, that's how popular
and competent he is.

19:28.167 --> 19:31.587
Anyway, you don't have to rush over there.
So just take your time, don't worry.

19:40.512 --> 19:41.805
We're at the tail-end

19:41.889 --> 19:43.015
of this long-term project.

19:43.098 --> 19:44.349
D-day is finally here, guys.

19:44.433 --> 19:46.226
Oh, that's right.

19:46.310 --> 19:48.270
We should go and grab something to eat

19:48.353 --> 19:51.106
before the others arrive at least.
That's how I believe we'll get through--

19:51.190 --> 19:52.774
- Good idea, except there's no time.
- He's right.

19:52.858 --> 19:54.776
Today is gonna be quite a hectic day.

19:54.860 --> 19:56.862
Why don't we conduct
our final meeting for this over lunch?

19:56.945 --> 19:58.739
I'll call and make the order right now.

19:58.822 --> 20:01.408
No, let me. You all good with sandwiches?

20:01.491 --> 20:02.576
- Yes.
- Hell yeah.

20:03.952 --> 20:05.204
Oh…

20:05.287 --> 20:08.540
Should… should I just get
the same thing for all of us?

20:08.624 --> 20:10.125
Actually, I'm on a diet.

20:10.209 --> 20:13.045
I'll have wheat bread, roast chicken,
olive oil, and pepper, please.

20:13.128 --> 20:15.005
I'd like the steak and cheese sub.
No pickles for me.

20:15.088 --> 20:17.007
- I can't ever eat pickles.
- And for me…

20:17.090 --> 20:19.509
What was that sauce we had
from the last time we ate?

20:19.593 --> 20:20.802
I wrote it down somewhere.

20:22.304 --> 20:24.556
All right, why don't you
let me do it instead?

20:24.640 --> 20:26.934
You'll have what you normally have, right?

20:27.017 --> 20:28.060
Sure.

20:37.069 --> 20:39.529
Ms. Kook, are you doing okay?
You've been looking quite exhausted.

20:39.613 --> 20:41.156
I'm all right.

20:41.865 --> 20:43.242
Like you asked us to do,

20:43.325 --> 20:44.910
we've organized two
separate press conferences

20:44.993 --> 20:46.245
for Nu-a and Go-oh later.

20:46.828 --> 20:48.789
We've estimated that Jean Ferrat
should be arriving

20:48.872 --> 20:50.374
around the time the drawing show ends.

20:50.457 --> 20:52.542
- He'll come straight from the airport.
- Okay. Thank you very much.

20:53.961 --> 20:56.838
Do you know what time
Go-oh will arrive here? Just an estimate?

20:58.590 --> 20:59.925
Wanna sleep over?

21:15.649 --> 21:16.942
Uhm, Ms. Kook?

21:18.151 --> 21:20.904
- Right. Don't worry. I'll ask him.
- Thanks.

21:22.030 --> 21:25.450
Oh, also, it looks like
Mr. Jang just arrived on the first floor.

21:25.534 --> 21:26.410
I see.

21:27.411 --> 21:28.370
Shouldn't you go greet him?

21:28.453 --> 21:29.955
I'll see him once this thing starts.

21:31.748 --> 21:34.668
Enjoy your meal, guys. We'll meet
at the front door in exactly 30 minutes.

21:34.751 --> 21:36.837
Gotta make some last-minute checks
on the second floor.

21:36.920 --> 21:37.879
- Okay. You got it.
- Understood.

21:40.340 --> 21:42.384
Today's interview is gonna be
about you as an artist.

21:42.467 --> 21:45.595
Your creative process. Feel free
to talk about your occupation and such.

21:45.679 --> 21:46.972
What do you mean? Like what?

21:47.055 --> 21:49.182
Like your thoughts
that are embedded in your work,

21:49.266 --> 21:51.810
your life in general
as a person who creates art for a living.

21:51.893 --> 21:53.520
Or maybe your goals
and plans for the future.

21:55.897 --> 21:56.898
I don't really have any.

21:58.275 --> 22:00.569
Can we just
skip to the next question, please?

22:00.652 --> 22:02.404
All right, then. Uh…

22:02.487 --> 22:05.365
Tell me how you began drawing.
Like, what moment got you into it?

22:12.873 --> 22:13.957
There's no story to tell.

22:16.001 --> 22:17.544
Okay, fine. You can say that then.

22:17.627 --> 22:20.255
Hold on. That's gonna
make him seem like a simpleton.

22:20.339 --> 22:21.298
Doesn't matter, it's the truth.

22:21.798 --> 22:23.467
No sugarcoating. Be true to yourself.

22:24.634 --> 22:25.761
Here we go.

22:29.681 --> 22:32.351
We're almost there now.

22:32.934 --> 22:33.810
Aren't you nervous?

22:34.978 --> 22:37.022
- Hmm?
- In a way, this is kinda like your debut.

22:37.105 --> 22:39.107
Your big introduction. Ta-da!

22:39.191 --> 22:42.027
Your very first public appearance. Crazy.
Aren't you nervous?

22:42.110 --> 22:43.904
If I say yes, are you gonna cancel it?

22:43.987 --> 22:45.530
No way in hell. Hang in there, dude.

22:46.281 --> 22:49.159
Oh, okay. I got just the song
for situations like this.

22:49.242 --> 22:52.287
Play "Island" by NJ, please.

22:55.248 --> 22:58.710
Oh, God, I'm so glad.
You're finally out of your cave.

22:59.294 --> 23:00.504
I was never in a cave, dumbass.

23:01.088 --> 23:02.964
You actually were. Don't deny it.

23:04.633 --> 23:07.719
To be honest, I was worried sick
that you'd have trouble sleeping,

23:07.803 --> 23:09.638
and you'd become even more
depressed and anxious

23:09.721 --> 23:11.973
ever since Yeon-su
came back into your life.

23:12.057 --> 23:14.768
But no need to mull over it.
In the end, this is all thanks to her.

23:14.851 --> 23:16.520
Future's looking even brighter now.

23:16.603 --> 23:18.814
You would have never done this
if I came up with it.

23:19.898 --> 23:21.942
Anyway, I hope you'll enjoy doing this

23:22.025 --> 23:24.820
and maybe even continue
working with others out in the open.

23:25.821 --> 23:28.407
Then you'll become
even more famous, get a lot more work,

23:28.490 --> 23:30.242
and rake in all the moolah.

23:32.035 --> 23:33.620
That being said, what's your take

23:33.703 --> 23:36.456
on giving your outstanding manager
a raise after this?

23:36.540 --> 23:37.749
I'm passionately against it.

23:37.833 --> 23:39.918
Hmm. I see. Then let's take our time

23:40.001 --> 23:42.212
and discuss that topic more
sometime down the road.

23:42.295 --> 23:44.089
- What?
- And here we are.

23:48.969 --> 23:50.762
Go and head up to the second floor first.

23:50.846 --> 23:52.139
Your green room will be there.

23:52.222 --> 23:53.932
I'll go look for parking,
and I'll bring your stuff over.

23:54.015 --> 23:56.643
You can forget about the raise.
You already have your welfare--

23:56.726 --> 23:59.563
Oh, boy, we're holding back the road.
Go on, they're getting angry back there.

24:00.564 --> 24:02.441
- See you later.
- All right, I'll see you soon.

24:26.423 --> 24:28.925
LIVE DRAWING SHOW

24:29.009 --> 24:32.137
LIVE DRAWING SHOW

24:35.348 --> 24:37.601
GO-OH, NU-A
SEON SHOP OPENING DRAWING SHOW

24:49.779 --> 24:52.699
GO-OH

25:01.041 --> 25:03.335
We should run it
by Ms. Kook before we do it.

25:04.002 --> 25:06.421
Mr. Kang, have you seen Ms. Kook?

25:06.505 --> 25:08.089
I saw her heading
to the second floor.

25:08.173 --> 25:10.342
- I see. Let's check the showroom.
- Okay.

25:49.965 --> 25:52.384
She always looked
perpetually mad whenever we're together.

25:57.556 --> 25:58.557
I think…

25:59.933 --> 26:02.477
I finally appreciate Yeon-su
for who she is.

26:16.032 --> 26:19.160
We already interviewed Ung this morning.
We just need Yeon-su's now.

26:19.244 --> 26:21.121
You don't need much,
just get some rough footage.

26:21.204 --> 26:23.498
Once the show begins,
make sure to focus on him.

26:23.582 --> 26:25.667
Intern, I want you to stay with her.

26:25.750 --> 26:27.294
Sure, you can count on that, sir.

26:27.377 --> 26:29.588
Should I interview her
before the event starts?

26:30.463 --> 26:31.548
No, I'll do it.

26:31.631 --> 26:33.717
We have a meeting
back at the office later,

26:33.800 --> 26:36.177
- so let's pick up the pace.
- Understood, sir.

26:53.278 --> 26:56.573
- Oh.
- I'm sorry, is this the waiting area?

26:57.616 --> 26:59.117
What the… It's Ung.

26:59.826 --> 27:01.036
When did he even get here?

27:17.469 --> 27:19.137
Great. What should I say?

27:19.721 --> 27:21.640
Do I wanna mention last night?

27:21.723 --> 27:22.891
About yesterday…

27:26.603 --> 27:27.979
You were at my place, right?

27:29.522 --> 27:30.732
I knew it.

27:31.566 --> 27:33.151
He doesn't remember at all.

27:35.695 --> 27:39.532
Yes. I had something to give you
so I went to your place.

27:40.325 --> 27:41.242
Hmm.

27:43.912 --> 27:45.372
Then did I do something--

27:45.455 --> 27:47.666
Oh, sorry.

27:47.749 --> 27:49.334
I need to get ready for the event.

27:49.417 --> 27:51.503
The staff will tell you the details
regarding the live show

27:51.586 --> 27:53.338
and everything else you need.

27:58.259 --> 28:02.263
But seriously, there's no reason
for me to be avoiding him like this.

28:03.390 --> 28:04.307
Hey.

28:06.559 --> 28:07.394
Good luck.

28:08.603 --> 28:09.479
Hmm.

28:22.325 --> 28:24.786
Oh, that's weird, you didn't run away.

28:24.869 --> 28:27.038
Take a rest, it's okay.
We'll just rehearse later.

28:27.122 --> 28:28.498
Here's the layout and program.

28:35.964 --> 28:37.382
LIVE DRAWING SHOW
GO-OH

28:38.591 --> 28:41.136
- Ms. Kook.
- Did you check Go-oh's video?

28:41.219 --> 28:43.138
Yes, I did. Everything's fine.
I checked the whole thing just now.

28:43.221 --> 28:45.765
Then go ahead and play it now, please,
alongside the playlist he's given us

28:45.849 --> 28:47.183
- and put it on a loop.
- Yep.

29:21.885 --> 29:23.136
Unbelievable.

29:24.179 --> 29:26.139
I've never seen that side of him before.

29:29.309 --> 29:30.477
Ms. Kook.

29:31.394 --> 29:32.604
Ms. Kook.

29:36.900 --> 29:37.901
Ms. Kook.

29:46.910 --> 29:48.369
Ung, we need to head out.

29:50.663 --> 29:51.706
Are you asleep?

29:54.250 --> 29:56.711
You feeling a little tense?
Do you want some more Xanax?

29:57.420 --> 29:58.421
Why…

30:00.381 --> 30:01.925
Why did I sleep well last night?

30:02.926 --> 30:05.762
You say that like it's a problem.
Are you still hung up on that?

30:05.845 --> 30:07.514
Yo, can you
write a caption for this?

30:07.597 --> 30:09.724
Can you write,
"Pondering about what to draw"?

30:09.808 --> 30:11.142
Make him look all mysterious.

30:11.726 --> 30:13.061
I think we can get a good view.

30:13.686 --> 30:15.313
Is this his? Which one?

30:15.396 --> 30:17.315
- No. It's the other one.
- This? Okay.

30:17.398 --> 30:18.525
Come on, let's go.

30:29.244 --> 30:31.329
- I won't see anything from here.
- Just sit down.

30:32.580 --> 30:34.415
- Come on.
- Let's sit at the front, right there.

30:35.792 --> 30:36.709
Nu-a is here.

30:42.090 --> 30:43.466
Hello. It's nice to meet you all.

30:44.133 --> 30:46.219
I'm honored to be able
to draw the buildings

30:46.302 --> 30:49.764
designed by my role model, Jean Ferrat,
more so in a setting such as this.

30:49.848 --> 30:51.266
I'm sure you're all aware,

30:51.349 --> 30:54.185
that another artist will be drawing
on the other side in parallel with me.

30:54.269 --> 30:56.980
So if you're curious, go ahead and peek.

30:57.063 --> 30:59.649
However, since you're already here,
I doubt any of you will.

30:59.732 --> 31:01.359
I guarantee you'll be
too immersed to move.

31:01.442 --> 31:04.654
I'll be doing my absolute best
to win your hearts as an illustrator.

31:04.737 --> 31:07.740
So now, ladies and gentlemen, I'm Nu-a.

31:12.787 --> 31:13.872
Hey, son!

31:19.127 --> 31:20.545
That's my son.

31:21.254 --> 31:23.840
- He's so good.
- Didn't think he'd be this tall.

33:06.067 --> 33:07.235
First time, huh?

33:07.318 --> 33:10.905
Uh-huh.

33:10.989 --> 33:12.949
I didn't know there was this side to him.

33:13.032 --> 33:14.826
He's like a different guy.

33:14.909 --> 33:16.285
Same here.

33:16.369 --> 33:19.622
He looked like a total stranger
the first time I saw him drawing.

33:19.706 --> 33:20.748
You're right.

33:22.333 --> 33:23.751
By the way, good job.

33:23.835 --> 33:27.422
This is quite a large-scale operation.
Must've been a pain to prepare this.

33:27.505 --> 33:29.132
No, really. All part of the work.

33:29.799 --> 33:32.677
Shouldn't you be working somewhere
instead of chatting with me?

33:32.760 --> 33:35.680
Exactly. I'm here to pick you up, Yeon-su.

33:38.182 --> 33:40.226
You can never judge a book by its cover.

33:40.309 --> 33:44.022
Who knew I'd be working side by side
with the lowest scoring kid?

33:44.605 --> 33:46.983
Obviously, he was
a nuisance all throughout.

33:47.066 --> 33:50.987
As you all know, we're incompatible.
He and I are strikingly different.

33:51.070 --> 33:52.822
Of course,
he's the annoying and frustrating type.

33:52.905 --> 33:55.491
During this project, he should've
shared his progress with me,

33:55.575 --> 33:57.660
so we'd be up to speed
to make things more efficient.

33:57.744 --> 33:59.495
But he never said a single word.

33:59.579 --> 34:00.872
Always just thinking to himself.

34:01.456 --> 34:02.915
He was always like that
from the beginning.

34:02.999 --> 34:05.126
I'd ask what was on his mind and it's,
"I don't know. Not sure.

34:05.209 --> 34:06.044
There's nothing to say."

34:06.127 --> 34:07.336
Either one of those.

34:08.421 --> 34:10.423
Great, I'm getting annoyed all over again.

34:10.506 --> 34:11.799
ANYTHING POSITIVE TO SAY ABOUT HIM?

34:11.883 --> 34:12.759
Nothing at all.

34:13.551 --> 34:14.552
Well…

34:14.635 --> 34:16.095
NOT EVEN ONE?

34:16.179 --> 34:19.223
I guess seeing him draw like that
for the first time kind of…

34:19.307 --> 34:22.477
it was like discovering
a new side of him I never noticed before.

34:23.644 --> 34:26.022
I mean, yes,
he used to draw a lot back then,

34:26.105 --> 34:28.775
but he never had
that serious look on his face before.

34:29.734 --> 34:32.612
I don't know what's gotten into him,
but he's completely focused,

34:32.695 --> 34:33.905
like he's in his element.

34:33.988 --> 34:35.740
Very different from the guy I know.

34:37.033 --> 34:38.326
But you know what?

34:38.409 --> 34:41.079
He was always serious about drawing,
it was his passion.

34:41.162 --> 34:43.289
If you check back,
I think it was in episode five,

34:43.372 --> 34:45.374
I accidentally ruined his drawing once,

34:45.458 --> 34:48.294
and he threw
a massive fit for days, like I hurt him.

34:48.377 --> 34:51.339
Honestly, I really did
feel bad about it. I did.

34:51.422 --> 34:54.300
But seeing him
all worked up was kind of entertaining.

34:54.884 --> 34:58.221
I mean, he rarely gets mad, you know.
He's always so quiet.

34:58.304 --> 34:59.639
I admit that I did tease him

34:59.722 --> 35:01.933
a few more times
to get a reaction for fun.

35:05.561 --> 35:07.438
He always made me laugh either way.

35:15.613 --> 35:16.697
Uhm…

35:17.532 --> 35:20.118
Yeah, basically
I'm not used to this side of him.

35:21.452 --> 35:24.664
I guess, it feels like he's changed.

35:27.208 --> 35:29.168
Funny, I thought he'd never change.

35:35.091 --> 35:38.427
Uhm, sorry, I was just rambling, wasn't I?
Let's cut that.

35:39.554 --> 35:41.848
- Okay, next question.
- Hmm.

36:03.369 --> 36:06.706
Huh. Shouldn't he
take a breather or something?

36:06.789 --> 36:09.625
Nah, this is how he always works.
All in till the end.

36:09.709 --> 36:13.045
But since there's an audience,
he probably feels even more tense.

36:14.589 --> 36:16.215
Good point. Let me go check up on him.

36:18.718 --> 36:21.262
- Honey, let's go.
- All right.

36:28.728 --> 36:32.023
Oh, wow. Is that you, Yeon-su?

36:32.106 --> 36:33.733
Hello, glad you're here.

36:33.816 --> 36:35.735
It's been ages since we saw each other.

36:35.818 --> 36:37.904
I heard you were
part of this project from the others.

36:37.987 --> 36:40.364
Yes. So how have you been lately?

36:40.448 --> 36:43.534
It's always the same for us.
Nothing's really changed.

36:43.618 --> 36:47.538
Goodness gracious. It's like
you haven't changed at all since then.

36:47.622 --> 36:49.207
Same goes for the both of you.

36:49.290 --> 36:51.125
Is it because of what we're wearing?

36:51.209 --> 36:53.419
Are you here to watch Ung's drawing show?

36:53.502 --> 36:54.754
Oh, yes, yes, yes.

36:54.837 --> 36:56.756
Then how come you're leaving already?

36:56.839 --> 36:59.383
Oh. It's kind of dragging, right?

36:59.467 --> 37:00.718
- No.
- That's not why.

37:01.427 --> 37:04.889
Seeing him draw all alone
like that, makes us feel uncomfortable.

37:04.972 --> 37:06.849
It reminds me
of the time when he was young.

37:07.558 --> 37:09.977
To think even back then
it was so normal for him--

37:10.061 --> 37:12.230
- We should get going, come on.
- Okay.

37:12.313 --> 37:14.523
Hey, Yeon-su,
come over for a meal sometime.

37:14.607 --> 37:16.442
- You know you're always welcome.
- Okay.

37:16.525 --> 37:18.861
No need to think about it too much,
just come on over.

37:18.945 --> 37:20.988
Don't worry, it's free of charge.

37:21.489 --> 37:22.907
He's right. You should come visit us.

37:22.990 --> 37:24.450
I'll make you something good.

37:24.533 --> 37:26.619
- Come, come.
- I'll be seeing you, okay?

37:39.465 --> 37:40.675
It's just that…

37:41.926 --> 37:44.053
the break-up devastated Ung.

37:45.471 --> 37:47.265
It must have been hard for you too.

37:54.188 --> 37:58.567
We really want you to visit us.
So please, come and drop by, okay?

37:58.651 --> 38:00.319
Okay. I will.

38:00.403 --> 38:01.904
All right. Goodbye.

38:02.488 --> 38:03.322
Mm-hmm.

38:04.156 --> 38:06.242
Come on. We have to go, Yeon-su.

38:06.325 --> 38:07.201
- Okay, okay.
- Hurry up.

38:07.285 --> 38:08.911
- Goodbye.
- Stop dragging your feet.

38:08.995 --> 38:10.454
Bye.

38:48.617 --> 38:49.744
- Ji-ung.
- Hm?

38:50.411 --> 38:51.871
Did you do the interview with Yeon-su?

38:51.954 --> 38:53.831
Yeah. And the shoot?

38:54.498 --> 38:56.125
There's nothing to film, so…

38:56.208 --> 38:58.586
Not like we'll get much,
he's been sitting down for hours.

38:58.669 --> 39:01.630
Go back to the office with Tae-hun,
start preparing for the meeting.

39:01.714 --> 39:03.841
Don't wait for me.
I'll wrap things up over here.

39:08.888 --> 39:12.016
It's just that
the break-up devastated Ung.

39:19.106 --> 39:20.316
Wanna sleep over?

39:27.573 --> 39:30.034
Are you sick? Do you have a fever?

39:46.467 --> 39:48.636
How many pills
did you take anyway?

39:49.387 --> 39:50.846
Do you take them often?

39:50.930 --> 39:53.224
Huh? When did you start taking them?

39:53.307 --> 39:56.727
Since when did you have trouble sleeping?
Why didn't you tell me much sooner?

40:29.135 --> 40:30.136
Yes?

40:31.387 --> 40:33.097
Oh, someone told me
that you were here.

40:33.180 --> 40:35.474
Everything's going well. In fact,
Nu-a's finishing up his piece now.

40:35.558 --> 40:37.268
Uh, escort him to the first floor.

40:37.351 --> 40:40.062
Get him all set up and prepped
for the press conference when he's done.

40:40.146 --> 40:41.730
Stay with him there.
I'll escort Go-oh myself.

40:41.814 --> 40:43.232
Got it, Ms. Kook.

41:00.249 --> 41:02.001
I still have a bit of time left.

41:04.378 --> 41:05.713
Hello, everyone.

41:05.796 --> 41:07.173
My name is Go-oh.

41:33.616 --> 41:34.700
Oh…

41:34.783 --> 41:36.285
Hey, you. Congratulations.

41:38.537 --> 41:39.872
You look a little different today.

41:43.626 --> 41:44.835
Wow, it's NJ!

42:02.228 --> 42:03.979
NJ.

42:23.415 --> 42:25.125
GO-OH, NU-A
SOEN SHOP OPENING DRAWING SHOW

42:25.709 --> 42:26.710
How's it going, Ms. Kook?

42:26.794 --> 42:28.504
How's everything?
It must have been a long day.

42:28.587 --> 42:30.464
Thank you so much for your work today.

42:30.548 --> 42:33.759
There's an after-party later, so feel free
to come, you're all invited to attend.

42:33.842 --> 42:36.387
Uh, I'll just wrap things up over here.
You can all go.

42:36.971 --> 42:39.390
Are you sure?
We can help you wrap up, we don't mind.

42:39.473 --> 42:42.726
It's okay. You had to work on the weekend.
You deserve to relax. Thank you. Go.

42:42.810 --> 42:44.728
Are you also coming to the after-party?

42:44.812 --> 42:46.939
I don't know yet. We'll see. Go ahead.

42:47.022 --> 42:48.732
All right, you have a good day, then.

42:48.816 --> 42:51.527
- Hope to see you later.
- You have to come, you deserve it too.

43:13.424 --> 43:16.218
Why the hell
isn't that jackass picking up his phone?

43:17.344 --> 43:18.470
Ung, over here! Come.

43:18.554 --> 43:20.097
Hey, why weren't you picking up?

43:20.180 --> 43:22.558
Hey, stranger.
All done with the press conference?

43:22.641 --> 43:24.184
NJ! What are you still doing here?

43:24.268 --> 43:26.770
Oh, I guess you're not excited to see me.

43:26.854 --> 43:29.398
Watch what you say next time,
you ungrateful fool.

43:29.481 --> 43:31.275
She personally made time
to see you all the way out here.

43:31.358 --> 43:33.527
Uh. Thank you so much
for coming to watch me.

43:33.611 --> 43:35.279
I didn't expect you to come here.

43:35.362 --> 43:36.947
I didn't think I'd come
uninvited to an event,

43:37.031 --> 43:38.449
just to see someone either.

43:38.532 --> 43:41.410
I actually arrived late
'cause of my schedule, but I still came.

43:41.493 --> 43:43.120
Gotta say, you looked different out there.

43:43.203 --> 43:45.205
NJ, I'll make extra sure
to send you an invite next time.

43:46.540 --> 43:49.460
Oh, right. Just a heads up,
in case you get all flustered

43:49.543 --> 43:51.962
seeing your name in
the top trending list in a few minutes,

43:52.046 --> 43:53.631
I told the reporters it's nothing weird.

43:53.714 --> 43:55.674
We're just two good friends
rooting for each other,

43:55.758 --> 43:56.967
so don't worry about anything.

43:57.551 --> 43:59.637
- Good friends?
- Well, yeah. Aren't we?

44:00.220 --> 44:01.513
Well, we… no, I…

44:01.597 --> 44:02.640
Yeah, of course we are.

44:03.432 --> 44:05.684
I'm just kinda flattered
you consider me as a friend.

44:06.935 --> 44:08.020
You're the first guy ever

44:08.103 --> 44:10.147
- who's happy to be friend-zoned by me.
- What?

44:10.230 --> 44:12.232
Never mind.

44:12.983 --> 44:14.485
Are you going home? Do you need a ride?

44:14.568 --> 44:16.111
It's okay.
We drove here as well. We'll be fine.

44:16.195 --> 44:17.529
Okay. You take care now.

44:17.613 --> 44:18.864
Sorry? Hold on.

44:18.947 --> 44:20.407
Is that the only reason
you were waiting for me?

44:20.491 --> 44:23.702
I already told you.
I'm very busy, but also I'm not.

44:23.786 --> 44:25.412
- Take care.
- Have a safe trip.

44:29.041 --> 44:30.459
Take care of yourself!

44:33.921 --> 44:36.423
Hey, Ung, how could you
decline her offer? What are you nuts?

44:36.507 --> 44:37.966
I'm exhausted. Shut up.

44:38.550 --> 44:41.387
- Anyway, this is pretty huge.
- What is?

44:41.470 --> 44:44.348
Today, you finally revealed yourself
to the adoring public,

44:44.431 --> 44:46.517
not to mention
instantly winning everyone's hearts.

44:46.600 --> 44:48.352
Bullshit. Just go and get the car, please.

44:48.936 --> 44:51.814
So by extension, this pretty much means
that you've agreed to give me a big raise.

44:51.897 --> 44:53.941
Shut up. I said, go and get the car.

44:55.609 --> 44:56.985
This was from NJ, right?

44:58.404 --> 45:00.614
Oh, my God, it smells different.

45:02.324 --> 45:04.743
Go-oh has finally debuted!

45:19.341 --> 45:20.300
That's sweet.

45:21.677 --> 45:22.845
God, you're so pathetic.

45:23.679 --> 45:26.807
Can't believe you're here to pity party
on such a freaking great day.

45:26.890 --> 45:29.476
What are you talking about?
I came in case you were bored.

45:30.477 --> 45:33.897
You got the bad juju.
Probably why this place is failing.

45:33.981 --> 45:35.274
You should be at that party

45:35.357 --> 45:37.943
celebrating the fact
that the project was a success!

45:38.026 --> 45:40.904
You actually passed with flying colors,
but instead, you're here sulking.

45:40.988 --> 45:42.990
- I like this more.
- This is beyond being pathetic.

45:43.073 --> 45:45.868
Aren't you ecstatic all that hard work
you've been doing paid off?

45:47.035 --> 45:49.872
Uh, not really. It's all just work.

45:49.955 --> 45:52.541
Now that we're done,
it's on to the next project.

45:55.294 --> 45:56.628
Things really tough at work?

45:57.296 --> 46:00.340
No. It's actually easier
compared to my old job.

46:01.091 --> 46:03.469
Yeah, I guess it's pretty good.

46:05.971 --> 46:07.181
Then what's the problem?

46:12.019 --> 46:14.354
It's not demanding enough to challenge me,

46:15.564 --> 46:16.940
not exactly fun either.

46:19.026 --> 46:21.695
That's all. Pretty much.

46:24.656 --> 46:25.824
Have another.

46:35.959 --> 46:37.336
Remember what you said?

46:38.212 --> 46:40.798
You said that my eyes
looked empty and soulless.

46:40.881 --> 46:42.174
There was nothing in them.

46:43.258 --> 46:44.802
Hmm. They're still the same.

46:44.885 --> 46:48.388
So empty that the fish I've got back there
have livelier eyes than you.

46:49.973 --> 46:54.728
Well, I saw this look in Ung's eyes
as he was drawing today.

46:56.396 --> 46:59.441
They seemed so animated.
Like they were so full of life.

47:02.277 --> 47:03.403
Really?

47:03.904 --> 47:04.905
Hmm.

47:05.989 --> 47:09.284
He was so focused on his drawing,
you could feel all his passion.

47:11.161 --> 47:12.621
To be honest, I was jealous.

47:13.831 --> 47:15.874
What exactly would you be jealous of?

47:17.209 --> 47:19.419
Do I sound pathetic?

47:19.503 --> 47:21.713
I always hated people
that I thought were pathetic.

47:22.798 --> 47:24.925
While he was working on improving himself,

47:25.425 --> 47:27.261
there I was, stagnant

47:27.344 --> 47:30.430
and busy making ends meet
with the soulless eyes of mine.

47:31.014 --> 47:33.350
Yup. Even I would think I'm pathetic.

47:34.017 --> 47:35.519
Christ. You're ridiculous.

47:36.270 --> 47:38.355
You weren't stagnating,
let alone being soulless.

47:38.438 --> 47:39.898
Think of the debt you had to pay off.

47:39.982 --> 47:42.150
Now that was tough,
I saw how hard you worked.

47:42.651 --> 47:43.610
Those are wins in life.

47:43.694 --> 47:46.029
And you've succeeded
by coming this far, you fool.

47:49.032 --> 47:51.326
Tonight I'm going to celebrate
a successful project.

47:51.410 --> 47:54.037
So consider me as your VIP.
Line up the soju bottles.

47:54.121 --> 47:56.748
- Okay, I already put nine on your tab.
- Really?

47:56.832 --> 47:59.042
Don't worry,
I'll be ripping you off all night.

47:59.960 --> 48:03.005
- Oh. Good evening.
- Hello, good evening.

48:04.006 --> 48:05.090
- Where?
- Over here?

48:05.173 --> 48:06.466
- Thank you.
- Okay.

48:12.681 --> 48:14.683
- Here's the menu.
- What's today's special?

48:14.766 --> 48:17.060
- Today, it's jjamppong rice.
- I'll have the bibimpap. No wait…

48:19.104 --> 48:20.981
Hey, Ung, good work today.

48:22.858 --> 48:25.068
I'm going home. You get some good rest.

48:25.569 --> 48:26.486
Hmm.

48:27.362 --> 48:30.657
Hey. On your way out,
can you turn off that light?

48:30.741 --> 48:32.910
All right. See ya.

48:32.993 --> 48:34.077
Hmm.

49:02.481 --> 49:03.732
And here's your order.

49:04.524 --> 49:06.318
- I'll take the empty bottles.
- Okay.

49:07.152 --> 49:09.738
Hey, you're here.
Sorry for calling out of the blue.

49:09.821 --> 49:12.407
I'm sure you know,
I'm pretty much the only friend she has.

49:12.491 --> 49:15.619
Unfortunately, I'm too busy tonight
I can't get rid of her myself.

49:15.702 --> 49:17.496
I can't hand her over
to the police either.

49:18.288 --> 49:21.416
She'll get mad when she wakes up.
Actually, who really cares.

49:21.500 --> 49:22.501
Take her.

49:23.335 --> 49:25.587
Yeah. One minute, please.

49:43.313 --> 49:44.147
That you, Ung?

49:57.995 --> 49:59.871
That's so cold.

50:03.834 --> 50:04.918
You awake yet?

50:10.924 --> 50:12.843
Didn't get enough rest?

50:12.926 --> 50:13.802
Uh-huh.

50:15.429 --> 50:17.180
On top of that,
I may have drunk a little bit.

50:17.764 --> 50:19.766
- I'm a little drunk.
- Drink this.

50:19.850 --> 50:21.810
Oh, how considerate.

50:29.276 --> 50:32.195
Sorry. What time is it?
Must have been a hassle.

50:32.279 --> 50:35.866
Not really.
I was at a boring get-together.

50:35.949 --> 50:38.076
- Did you drink too?
- A little bit.

50:38.160 --> 50:39.202
But you're a lightweight.

50:40.704 --> 50:42.914
- You remember that?
- Of course I do.

50:42.998 --> 50:45.208
Like watching a grown man
who couldn't handle baby sips.

50:46.543 --> 50:47.544
Okay, that's a stretch.

50:55.677 --> 50:58.847
By the way,
how's the documentary going anyway?

50:58.930 --> 51:01.016
Well, it's going okay.

51:01.600 --> 51:04.186
I regret agreeing to do it again
after all these years.

51:04.811 --> 51:07.773
Back in high school, at least we were
young and cute, which was fine to watch.

51:07.856 --> 51:10.025
But now all they're gonna get
is a bunch of adults working.

51:10.108 --> 51:11.526
It'll just be boring.

51:12.527 --> 51:14.821
I'm afraid this whole thing
is gonna be a flop.

51:14.905 --> 51:16.281
Sounds like wishful thinking on your part.

51:16.364 --> 51:18.575
So? I'll make sure
no one ever gets to watch it.

51:18.658 --> 51:20.619
You know how I am at promoting things.

51:20.702 --> 51:24.581
I'm going to spread a rumor.

51:27.459 --> 51:30.712
But if you agree to let me watch it first,
I might change my mind.

51:31.880 --> 51:34.549
- You wanna watch it?
- I may have looked ugly in some shots

51:34.633 --> 51:36.968
or blurted out
a swear word or two without realizing it.

51:37.052 --> 51:40.138
I'm pretty sure that Ung
was talking crap about me all throughout.

51:41.223 --> 51:44.226
Anyway, just curious. That's all.

51:49.439 --> 51:52.234
By the way, what did Ung say about me?

51:52.776 --> 51:53.777
Was it all bad?

52:01.243 --> 52:02.244
I mean…

52:03.245 --> 52:04.871
- Did he just shit-talk about--
- Hey…

52:07.666 --> 52:09.209
You still like him, don't you?

52:23.682 --> 52:26.601
Hey.
You still like him, don't you?

52:28.145 --> 52:29.688
No. That's impossible.

52:43.910 --> 52:45.704
There's no way this is happening.

52:45.787 --> 52:46.830
Choi Ung?

52:52.419 --> 52:54.129
What are you doing out here so late?

52:54.880 --> 52:57.966
I found out
that you moved back here recently.

52:59.509 --> 53:01.469
I guess that's why
we kept running into each other.

53:02.053 --> 53:03.972
Oh, I guess.

53:06.391 --> 53:07.684
Did you have a drink?

53:08.268 --> 53:10.687
What? Uh…

53:11.271 --> 53:12.439
Hmm.

53:13.398 --> 53:15.942
I did. Anyway, what are you
doing out here? It's kinda late.

53:17.569 --> 53:18.987
Yeah, I guess.

53:19.070 --> 53:21.323
It was already late
when I got here earlier,

53:21.406 --> 53:23.783
so I was debating
if maybe I should just go.

53:24.743 --> 53:25.577
Uh…

53:26.411 --> 53:29.206
If it's not that urgent,
maybe we can just talk next time?

53:29.289 --> 53:30.582
I'm really tired right now.

54:39.317 --> 54:40.694
Hey, it's you again.

54:46.157 --> 54:47.325
Am I dreaming?

54:56.042 --> 54:57.294
I won't fall for it.

55:03.091 --> 55:04.175
Yeon-su.

55:14.227 --> 55:15.812
I've been in so much pain.

55:29.993 --> 55:32.662
No, I remember all of it.

55:33.246 --> 55:35.874
You okay? You seem pretty wasted.

55:37.292 --> 55:38.877
No, I'm fine. I'm just tired.

55:42.630 --> 55:43.715
You…

55:45.467 --> 55:46.301
About last night…

55:48.928 --> 55:52.432
Well, I saw a Thermos bottle at my house.

55:52.515 --> 55:53.975
I was wondering if you left it there.

55:55.268 --> 55:58.063
Thank God.
I'm glad he doesn't remember anything.

55:59.773 --> 56:03.443
Yes. You kind of seemed like you were
out of it, so I just left it there.

56:05.153 --> 56:06.488
Oh, really?

56:06.571 --> 56:10.575
Mm-hmm. You were on some pills.
All dazed and stuff.

56:11.451 --> 56:13.536
Did I fall asleep right after you left?

56:14.829 --> 56:15.830
I think so.

56:18.625 --> 56:20.668
Oh, okay then.

56:21.586 --> 56:23.421
Did you come all the way here
to ask me that?

56:24.255 --> 56:25.632
You could've just called.

56:30.637 --> 56:32.722
Looks like
I'm the only one who'll remember.

56:33.973 --> 56:35.308
I should go inside now.

56:36.017 --> 56:37.143
See ya.

56:37.727 --> 56:39.854
Guess I'll just take it to my grave.

56:39.938 --> 56:43.316
Tomorrow, you should
just pretend that you don't remember.

56:46.319 --> 56:47.487
It wasn't a dream.

56:52.242 --> 56:53.576
There's no need to lie.

56:58.373 --> 56:59.582
So why pretend?

57:01.668 --> 57:02.752
Yeon-su.

57:10.009 --> 57:11.010
Yeon-su.

57:28.153 --> 57:29.487
Do you think this is right?

57:33.283 --> 57:35.452
Do you think
what we're doing right now is right?

57:47.005 --> 57:49.424
We're not like everyone else. We're us.

57:53.219 --> 57:55.180
Our love for each other wasn't lukewarm…

57:58.725 --> 58:00.643
and in the same way,
neither was our breakup.

58:02.687 --> 58:04.355
It's been way too long.

58:06.191 --> 58:07.775
We should be able to…

58:10.570 --> 58:12.155
…ask each other "How have you been?"

58:13.615 --> 58:14.949
"How tough has it been for you?"

58:16.910 --> 58:19.662
"It's been tough for me."
We're allowed to say those things.

58:23.291 --> 58:24.876
The reason we broke up…

58:28.713 --> 58:29.797
How have you been?

58:30.673 --> 58:32.759
…it was because I was arrogant.

58:32.842 --> 58:34.093
Answer me.

58:35.887 --> 58:37.013
How have you been, Yeon-su?

58:38.097 --> 58:40.433
I was so arrogant,
I thought I could live…

58:42.644 --> 58:43.770
without you.

58:57.158 --> 59:04.165
PRIDE AND PREJUDICE

59:25.937 --> 59:28.189
I'm going to keep that as a hobby.

59:28.273 --> 59:31.150
What I want
is to bask in the sun during the day

59:31.234 --> 59:33.486
and lay underneath a lamp at night time.

59:33.570 --> 59:35.321
A stressful life just isn't for me.

59:36.197 --> 59:37.031
I'll be right back.

59:41.536 --> 59:43.538
I sounded pathetic didn't I?

59:49.836 --> 59:53.172
JOBS FOR DESIGN MAJORS

59:55.758 --> 59:56.759
HOW EASY IS IT TO GET A JOB?

59:56.843 --> 59:58.636
MAKING MONEY THROUGH DRAWING

01:00:00.013 --> 01:00:02.932
4 MONTHS AFTER THE BREAKUP
